Emma: Yes, please. It''s my first time eating real Chinese food.
Waiter: Then let me suggest a few dishes. Do you like spicy food?
Emma: A little, but not too hot. I get scared of very spicy dishes.
Waiter: How about steamed fish and some fried rice with eggs?
Emma: That sounds lovely. Should I order rice for everyone?
Waiter: Yes. In China we usually share the dishes and each have our own bowl of rice.
Emma: I see. So everyone takes a little from each plate. What a nice custom!', 'Emma 第一次吃正宗中餐,请服务员推荐;服务员问她吃不吃辣,她说只能吃一点;服务员推荐清蒸鱼和蛋炒饭;并解释中餐通常是大家共享菜肴、各自一碗米饭。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Emma ask the waiter for suggestions?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It is her first time eating real Chinese food.","She has no money.","She cannot read the menu at all.","She is in a hurry to leave."]},{"q":"How does Emma feel about spicy food?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She loves the hottest dishes.","She can eat only a little, not too hot.","She refuses all Chinese food.","She has never heard of it."]},{"q":"What two dishes does the waiter suggest?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Steamed fish and fried rice with eggs.","Cold soup and sweet cake.","Spicy noodles and ice cream.","Bread and butter pudding."]},{"q":"How are the dishes usually eaten in China, according to the waiter?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Each person orders one separate dish.","Everyone shares the dishes with their own bowl of rice.","People eat in complete silence.","Only the host eats first."]},{"q":"What is Emma''s reaction to the custom?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She finds it rude.","She wants to leave at once.","She thinks it is a nice custom.","She refuses to share."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U3', 'sufe');
In some places, it is rude to turn a fish over on the plate, because people believe it brings bad luck.
In China and Japan, you should never stand your chopsticks straight up in a bowl of rice.
In parts of the Middle East, people use only their right hand to touch food.
Learning these small rules before you travel shows respect for the local culture.', '每个国家都有自己的就餐习俗,常令游客吃惊;有的地方认为把鱼翻面会带来坏运气;在中国和日本,不要把筷子直插在米饭里;中东部分地区只用右手碰食物;出行前了解这些小规矩是对当地文化的尊重。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"In some places, why should you not turn a fish over?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It makes the fish too cold.","The waiter has to clean it.","It costs extra money.","People believe it brings bad luck."]},{"q":"What should you never do with chopsticks in China and Japan?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Stand them straight up in a bowl of rice.","Use them to eat rice.","Hold them in your right hand.","Wash them before eating."]},{"q":"In parts of the Middle East, which hand is used to touch food?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only the left hand.","Only the right hand.","Both hands together.","Neither hand at all."]},{"q":"What is the main message of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Travelling abroad is dangerous.","All countries eat the same way.","Learning local rules shows respect for the culture.","Dining customs never change."]},{"q":"Who might be surprised by these customs?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only local children.","Only restaurant owners.","Nobody at all.","A visitor from another country."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U3', 'sufe');
Lin: Sure. When you sit down, wait for the host to start the meal first.
Tom: Got it. And should I finish everything in my bowl?
Lin: Actually, if you finish it all, the host may think you want more food.
Tom: Really? At home I was taught to clean my plate to be polite.
Lin: Here it''s the opposite. Leaving a little shows you are full and satisfied.
Tom: That''s so different! Anything else I should know?
Lin: Just relax and enjoy. They''ll be happy that you try their food with an open mind.', 'Tom 明天去中国朋友家做客,向 Lin 请教餐桌礼仪;Lin 说要等主人先动筷;吃光碗里的饭主人会以为你还想要;在中国留一点反而表示吃饱了、满意了;最后建议他放松享受、以开放心态尝试。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Tom ask Lin for advice?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He is visiting a Chinese friend''s home.","He is opening a restaurant.","He is writing a cookbook.","He cannot find the address."]},{"q":"What does Lin say to do when you sit down?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Begin eating immediately.","Wait for the host to start the meal first.","Leave the table quickly.","Ask for the bill."]},{"q":"What might the host think if Tom finishes everything?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["That Tom is angry.","That Tom is leaving.","That Tom wants more food.","That Tom dislikes the meal."]},{"q":"What does leaving a little food show in China?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["That the food is bad.","That you are still hungry.","That you want to pay.","That you are full and satisfied."]},{"q":"What is Lin''s final piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Relax and try the food with an open mind.","Eat as fast as possible.","Bring your own food.","Refuse anything new."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U3', 'sufe');
A single smell or taste can bring back a whole afternoon at our grandmother''s table.
When we feel tired or sad as adults, we often look for these comfort foods.
They remind us of family, of home and of being cared for.
In this way, a simple dish can carry far more meaning than just a meal.', '我们许多人把最爱的食物与童年的快乐记忆相连;一种气味或味道就能唤回在奶奶餐桌旁的整个下午;长大后疲惫或难过时,我们常会寻找这些慰藉食物;它们让我们想起家人、家和被照顾的感觉;这样,一道简单的菜承载的意义远不止一顿饭。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many people connect their favourite foods with?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The price of restaurants.","Happy memories from childhood.","Famous chefs on television.","Long journeys abroad."]},{"q":"What can a single smell or taste bring back?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A list of new recipes.","The cost of the meal.","A whole afternoon at grandmother''s table.","A map of the city."]},{"q":"When do adults often look for comfort foods?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only on their birthdays.","When they are very rich.","Only during exams.","When they feel tired or sad."]},{"q":"What do these foods remind people of?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Family, home and being cared for.","Their school timetable.","The weather outside.","The latest news."]},{"q":"What is the main idea of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cooking is a waste of time.","A simple dish can carry deep meaning.","Comfort food is unhealthy.","Memories have nothing to do with food."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U3', 'sufe');
Jack: Good idea. What do you feel like eating?
Mia: Maybe something warm. How about noodle soup?
Jack: Sounds great. I''ll get boiled dumplings too, with a little vinegar.
Mia: Perfect. Can you ask them to make mine less salty?
Jack: Sure. The shop near us has fresh, homemade noodles.
Mia: Lovely. How long will it take to arrive?
Jack: About thirty minutes. Let''s set the table while we wait.', 'Mia 太累不想做饭,提议点外卖;Jack 同意,问她想吃什么;Mia 想吃热乎的面汤;Jack 还想点水煮饺子配点醋;Mia 请他让自己的少放盐;附近店有新鲜手工面;大约三十分钟送到,两人先摆好餐桌。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Mia want to order takeaway?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The kitchen is broken.","She has no food at all.","She is too tired to cook.","She is having a party."]},{"q":"What warm dish does Mia choose?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Cold salad.","Sweet cake.","Fried eggs.","Noodle soup."]},{"q":"What does Jack want to order in addition?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Boiled dumplings with vinegar.","A pot of coffee.","Some ice cream.","A loaf of bread."]},{"q":"What does Mia ask them to do with her food?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Make it much hotter.","Make it less salty.","Add more sugar.","Cut it into pieces."]},{"q":"How long will the food take to arrive?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["About three hours.","About five minutes.","About thirty minutes.","The whole evening."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U3', 'sufe');
Chinese cooks often try to balance many flavours in one meal.
They mix salty, spicy, sour, sweet and bitter tastes in a careful way.
A colourful plate of vegetables, meat and rice gives the body what it needs.
Eating a variety of fresh foods is one simple secret of staying healthy.', '一顿好饭应既有营养又赏心悦目;中国厨师常努力在一餐中平衡多种味道;把咸、辣、酸、甜、苦仔细调和;一盘色彩丰富的蔬菜、肉和米饭能给身体所需;吃多样的新鲜食物是保持健康的一个简单秘诀。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What should a good meal be, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only very cheap.","Only very spicy.","Cooked very quickly.","Both nutritious and appealing to the eye."]},{"q":"What do Chinese cooks often try to balance?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Many flavours in one meal.","The price of each dish.","The size of the table.","The number of guests."]},{"q":"Which five tastes are mentioned?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Hot, cold, warm, fresh and old.","Salty, spicy, sour, sweet and bitter.","Red, green, blue, white and black.","Big, small, long, short and round."]},{"q":"What gives the body what it needs?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A bowl of plain water.","A single piece of cake.","A colourful plate of vegetables, meat and rice.","A cup of black coffee."]},{"q":"What is one simple secret of staying healthy?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Eating only one kind of food.","Skipping every meal.","Eating very late at night.","Eating a variety of fresh foods."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U3', 'sufe');

